      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_present",
      "impact_statement": "CVE-2026-106070 is in the zlib.ZipFile API, which can return attacker-controlled bytes for an entry after local and central ZIP header validation fails. The October 2026 advisory lists only Node.js 26.x as affected (https://nodejs.org/en/blog/vulnerability/october-2026-security-releases); the fix, https://github.com/nodejs/node/commit/745ad77156 (zlib: avoid caching invalid ZIP local headers), changes lib/internal/zip/entry.js on the 26.x line. The 24.x line has no zlib.ZipFile: lib/zlib.js in v24.22.0 and v24.22.3 does not define it, and lib/internal/zip does not exist there. We checked the node binary in every published nodejs-24 package for Debian 13 in the DHI Debian repository (24.16.0-0 to the current 24.22.3-0, amd64 and arm64) for the embedded internal/zip/entry module: it is absent from every build, while the embedded internal/dns/callback_resolver module, checked the same way, is present in each."
